 "_meta": {
  "bed": "local ERPNext dev bed, v15.94.3 (frappe 15.96.0), Standard chart of accounts, IDR",
  "recorded": "2026-11-16",
  "ticket": "#1599",
  "about": "ECX8-T0: Payment Entry against a party balance created by an opening entry, with no invoice",
  "names": "synthetic: company \"ECX Probe Co\" (abbr EPC), parties and employees named \"ECX Probe ...\" / \"Probe ...\", bed users replaced by role labels",
  "apiUsers": {
   "apiUserWithSystemManager": "token-auth API user holding the 901-bot role set (Accounts Manager/User, Purchase Manager/User, Stock Manager/User, Sales Manager/User, Projects Manager/User, System Manager) plus HR Manager/User and, from the Supplier probe on, Purchase Master Manager",
   "apiUserWithoutSystemManager": "same roles minus System Manager (and without Purchase Master Manager)"
  },
  "notes": [
   "Body: POST /api/resource/Payment Entry {payment_type:\"Pay\", company, posting_date, party_type, party, paid_from, paid_to, paid_amount, received_amount, reference_no:<key>, reference_date}, then PUT {docstatus:1}. No references rows.",
   "Confirmed: an unallocated payment against supplier A (opening credit 5000000, payment 2000000) leaves get_balance_on = -3000000: the opening party balance falls by exactly the payment. Its Payment Ledger Entry is against the Payment Entry itself (an advance), GL rows: credit bank, debit Creditors with the party, is_opening No.",
   "Alternative: references:[{reference_doctype:\"Journal Entry\", reference_name:<opening JE>, allocated_amount}] is accepted; the Payment Ledger Entry is then against the Journal Entry, unallocated_amount 0, and the balance falls by the same amount. Allocation above the entry outstanding -> 417 ValidationError \"Row #1: Allocated Amount cannot be greater than outstanding amount.\"",
   "Paying more than the balance is NOT refused: supplier B, opening 700000, 200000 allocated to the JE then 900000 unallocated: balance +400000 (a debit balance).",
   "Employee party on a Creditors account works: opening 300000 credit, payment 100000: balance -200000.",
   "Bank paid_from: reference_no and reference_date are mandatory at save (417 ValidationError \"Reference No and Reference Date is mandatory for Bank transaction\"); a Cash paid_from needs neither.",
   "Save is permissive: a non-bank paid_from, a non-payable paid_to, missing paid_to, paid vs received mismatch (same currency), a Customer party on a payable account and a posting date outside any year all SAVE as drafts. Submit refuses: P&L paid_from without a cost centre (417 \"Cost Center is required for Profit and Loss account\"), paid_to a Cash account with a party (417 \"Party Type and Party can only be set for Receivable / Payable account\"), no covering year (FiscalYearError). Missing paid_to, mismatch and Customer-on-payable SUBMIT fine: PMO must send paid_to, equal amounts and the right party type itself.",
   "reference_no is NOT unique (a second payment with the same reference_no saves and submits). Lookup before create: GET Payment Entry with filters [company, reference_no].",
   "Missing party -> 417 \"Party is mandatory\"; unknown party -> 417 LinkValidationError; zero paid_amount -> 417 \"Paid Amount is mandatory\".",
   "Payment Entry create and submit work for a user without System Manager."
  ],
  "v16": "identical in behaviour; read-back method differs (get_balance_on not whitelisted); remarks text differs"
 },
 "observations": [
  "supplier A balance before -5000000, after unallocated 2000000 payment -3000000",
  "supplier B: opening 700000 credit; after 200000 allocated to the opening entry -500000; after a further 900000 unallocated +400000",
  "employee: opening 300000 credit; after 100000 unallocated -200000"
 ],
